<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kremnica</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Körmöcbánya, Kremnitz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kremnica is a mining town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, called Körmöcbánya in the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>. Its gold mines made it one of the richest towns in the kingdom, and the mint founded there in 1328 struck the Hungarian gold florin and later ducats. The mint still operates, making it one of the oldest continuously working mints in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kremnica.jpg" alt="Kremnica" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dušan Turan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kremnica_v_zime.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
